# This file is a configuration reference; devicerail-daemon never loads it
# automatically. Inject selected variables with the host shell, service manager,
# container runtime, or Windows service configuration. On POSIX, export each
# selected setting (plain sourcing does not export these assignments); in
# PowerShell use $env:NAME = "value".

# DeviceRail defaults to stdio. Uncomment only when a loopback TCP control
# endpoint is explicitly required; non-loopback addresses are rejected.
# DEVICERAIL_RPC_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:47831

# These two owner-only files jointly enable the optional pre-hello HMAC gate on
# the JSON-RPC listener. They are invalid without DEVICERAIL_RPC_LISTEN and do
# not authenticate the separate distributed peer-v2 listener.
# DEVICERAIL_RPC_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/owner-only/rpc-credentials.json
# DEVICERAIL_RPC_AUDIT_LOG=/absolute/owner-only/rpc-audit.jsonl

DEVICERAIL_EVIDENCE_DIR=.devicerail/evidence
DEVICERAIL_ANDROID=auto
# DEVICERAIL_ADB_PATH=adb

# HarmonyOS defaults to off and does not resolve or invoke HDC. Set auto to
# attempt one startup discovery while preserving other routes after HDC failure
# or an empty inventory. Set required to fail daemon startup on initialization,
# discovery, an empty inventory, or registration conflict. HDC_PATH is valid
# only with auto|required and otherwise defaults to the separately installed hdc.
DEVICERAIL_HARMONY=off
# DEVICERAIL_HDC_PATH=hdc
DEVICERAIL_SCREENSHOT_POLICY=capture

# Legacy external iOS mode is disabled unless the WDA endpoint and stable
# device token are both present. It accepts only explicit numeric loopback HTTP;
# the operator starts WDA and iproxy.
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_WDA_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8100
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_DEVICE_TOKEN=00008030-001
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_DEVICE_NAME="Lab iPhone"
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_OS_VERSION=18.0
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_MJPEG_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9100

# Managed discovery merges physical devices from devicectl/xcdevice with
# available Simulators from simctl; only a Booted Simulator is connected.
# DEVICE_TOKEN may select either kind. Without it, the unique connected physical
# device is preferred, then the unique Booted Simulator. DeviceRail does not
# create or boot Simulators. auto keeps discovering after startup; required
# fails startup.
#
# Managed Direct WDA caches a WDA build and supervises xcodebuild. A physical
# target also uses signing, trust/Developer Mode checks, and iproxy. A Simulator
# skips those steps and shares WDA's selected host-local port directly. Run
# `devicerail-daemon ios doctor` first. Physical-device Apple security prompts
# remain user-confirmed.
# DEVICERAIL_IOS=auto
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_BACKEND=direct-wda
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_DEVICE_TOKEN=<physical-or-simulator-UDID>
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_WDA_PROJECT=/absolute/path/to/WebDriverAgent.xcodeproj
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_DERIVED_DATA=.devicerail/ios/DerivedData
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_IPROXY_PATH=iproxy
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_WDA_LOCAL_PORT=0
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_WDA_REMOTE_PORT=8100
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_ALLOW_PROVISIONING_UPDATES=false

# Appium mode uses an operator-installed Appium/XCUITest Driver. Select exactly
# one numeric-loopback endpoint or executable. With DEVICERAIL_IOS=auto|required
# and no WDA project, DeviceRail discovers a physical device or Booted Simulator
# while XCUITest Driver owns its bundled WDA. SESSION_TARGET defaults to native;
# safari is valid only with the Appium backend. The managed executable is
# launched only with fixed address, port, and base-path arguments.
# DEVICERAIL_IOS=auto
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_BACKEND=appium
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_SESSION_TARGET=native
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_APPIUM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4723
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_APPIUM_PATH=/absolute/path/to/appium
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_APPIUM_PORT=0
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_APPIUM_BASE_PATH=/
# Typed appium:newCommandTimeout; defaults to 600 and accepts only 1..=3600.
# DEVICERAIL_IOS_APPIUM_NEW_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600

# Native Desktop control is disabled by default. auto preserves the other
# routes after discovery/registration failure; required fails daemon startup.
# One daemon registers only the native route for its compile-time host, and
# inventory is lazy: connect performs the first runtime desktop probe.
DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP=off
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_ID=desktop-local
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_NAME="Local desktop"
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_OS_VERSION=14.5
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# macOS: grant Screen Recording and Accessibility to devicerail-daemon itself.
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_MACOS_SCREENCAPTURE=/usr/sbin/screencapture

# Windows: run devicerail-daemon in the intended interactive user session.
# A Session 0 service cannot capture or control a logged-in user's desktop.
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_WINDOWS_POWERSHELL=powershell.exe

# Linux: select x11 or wayland explicitly, or leave this unset for closed
# XDG_SESSION_TYPE/DISPLAY/WAYLAND_DISPLAY detection. Automatic detection cannot
# enable Wayland because its explicit mode and complete viewport are mandatory.
# X11 also needs matching DISPLAY/XAUTHORITY access.
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_LINUX_DISPLAY_SERVER=x11
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_X11_IMPORT=import
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_X11_XDOTOOL=xdotool

# Wayland requires DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_LINUX_DISPLAY_SERVER=wayland,
# WAYLAND_DISPLAY, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, grim, and the complete physical-pixel
# viewport below. auto prefers ydotool and then wtype; ydotool also requires a
# separately running ydotoold with /dev/uinput access.
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_WAYLAND_GRIM=grim
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_WAYLAND_INPUT=auto
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_WAYLAND_YDOTOOL=ydotool
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_WAYLAND_WTYPE=wtype
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_WAYLAND_VIEWPORT_WIDTH=1920
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_WAYLAND_VIEWPORT_HEIGHT=1080
# DEVICERAIL_DESKTOP_WAYLAND_VIEWPORT_SCALE_FACTOR=1.0

# Playwright is disabled unless an endpoint is present. The separately built
# helper and a compatible Node.js runtime are required when it is enabled.
# DEVICERAIL_PLAYWRIGHT_ENDPOINT=ws://127.0.0.1:3000/session-token
# DEVICERAIL_PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSER=chromium
# DEVICERAIL_PLAYWRIGHT_NODE=node
# DEVICERAIL_PLAYWRIGHT_HELPER=/absolute/path/to/helper.js

# RDP is disabled unless all required settings are present. Never commit the
# token to a config file; inject it from a local secret store at runtime.
# DEVICERAIL_RDP_BRIDGE=127.0.0.1:47832
# DEVICERAIL_RDP_TARGET=rdp://host.example:3389
# DEVICERAIL_RDP_TOKEN=REPLACE_AT_RUNTIME
# DEVICERAIL_RDP_NAME=lab-desktop

# Process plugins are disabled unless an absolute platform path list is set.
# Unix discovery requires owner-only/no-follow manifests and executables;
# platforms where an equivalent ACL and file identity cannot be proved fail
# closed. The optional timeout is valid only when plugin directories are set.
# DEVICERAIL_PLUGIN_DIRS=/absolute/owner-only/plugins
# DEVICERAIL_PLUGIN_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# Distributed routing has independent outbound and inbound opt-ins. Each value
# names a bounded owner-only/no-follow JSON file, not inline JSON. The outbound
# file declares mandatory loopback terminations of operator-managed SSH/mTLS
# tunnels; one missing or incompatible peer fails the whole startup set.
# DEVICERAIL_DISTRIBUTED_PEERS=/absolute/owner-only/distributed-peers.json

# The server file has exactly schemaVersion, nodeId, listen,
# securityMode="externalSshOrMtls", tunnelId, nodeEpoch, and
# inventoryRevision. listen must be a numeric loopback address with a non-zero
# port; epoch/revision are positive JavaScript-safe integers. Raw loopback TCP
# has no built-in authentication, and RPC credentials do not protect peer-v2.
# The external SSH/mTLS tunnel and exclusive local termination are operator
# responsibilities. The listener's starting gate permits discovery but returns
# retryable node_starting for leases/mutations until outbound registration is
# ready. Non-Unix owner-only configuration currently fails closed.
# DEVICERAIL_DISTRIBUTED_SERVER=/absolute/owner-only/distributed-server.json
